I like that idea a lot!  I don't think it should be a hard limit though, 
otherwise you'd eventually hit a limit where you can no longer sacrifice 
anything.  The limit would work like so: you have a huge array of integers 
for each monster.  Each time you sacrifice a monster, its array entry is 
incremented, and when it passes 40, further sacrifices of that type are 
ignored.  At the same time, for every corpse that you sacrifice, one of the 
nonzero integers in the array is randomly decremented.  So if you keep on 
sacrificing puddings you'll quickly hit the limit, but if you then 
sacrifice a lot of other stuff, you'll be able to sacrifice more puddings 
again.


